  "headline": "Expansion of Sekolah Rakyat Program Continues Across Indonesia",
  "seoTitle": "Sekolah Rakyat Program Address Out of School Youth",
  "metaDescription": "Government officials push for the Sekolah Rakyat program expansion, including new facilities in Humbang Hasundutan to address high dropout rates nationwide.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The Humbang Hasundutan regional government proposed a permanent Sekolah Rakyat facility on a six-hectare plot to support children from low-income families.",
    "Data indicates over 437,000 children in West Java are currently out of school, prompting calls for local leaders to increase parental awareness.",
    "The Ministry of Social Affairs is reviewing Ombudsman findings regarding institutional standards and student enrollment procedures within the program."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Sekolah Rakyat initiative is undergoing a national expansion as part of efforts to improve educational access and achieve Sustainable Development Goals. Recent developments include a proposal from the Humbang Hasundutan regency in North Sumatra to establish a permanent school facility on six hectares of land. Simultaneously, officials have highlighted the need to address high numbers of children currently not attending school, with reports noting over 437,000 children affected in West Java alone. To manage these facilities, the government is emphasizing the roles of guardians and dormitory wardens, referring to them as essential for the success of the program. Meanwhile, oversight bodies including the Ombudsman are reviewing the operational standards and management of child social welfare institutions and their integration with the Sekolah Rakyat system to ensure effective service delivery for the targeted demographic.",
